{title: Sent Eastward}
{subtitle: Genesis 25:1–2; 25:5–6; 25:7–10; 1 Chronicles 1:32–33}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 85}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] |
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] | [Bb] [C] |
| [Dm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Abraham took another [F]wife
Her name was Ke[C]turah
She [Dm]bore him Zimran [F]first
With five other [C]sons named
Jokshan Me[Bb]dan and Midian
Ishbak and [Dm]Shuah
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Everything to [F]Isaac
But gifts to the [C]rest
Sent away [Bb]eastward
Away from the [Dm]west
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
While he was still a[F]live
He sent them to the [C]land
Where the [Dm]sun rises ear[F]ly
Far from Isaac's [C]hand
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Dm] | [Dm] |
| [Dm] | [F] | [C] | [C] | ×2
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Dm] | [Dm] | ×2

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Abraham breathed his [F]last
Old and satisfied with [C]life
[Dm]Gathered to his people
[F]His days were [C]done
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Isaac and [Bb]Ishmael
Buried him in the [Dm]cave
In the field of Ep[Bb]hron
Facing [Dm]Mamre
{end_of_verse}
